@startuml
title Stage 0.5 - FrameMetadata Lifecycle (Ownership + Release Chain)

skinparam shadowing false

[*] --> Allocated : FrameMetadataStore.acquire()

Allocated --> Filled : Decode fills buffer\nand sets timestamps
Filled --> Enqueued1 : push to Queue1
Enqueued1 --> Dequeued1 : DummyDetection pop

Dequeued1 --> Detected : ObjectMetadata handles attached\n+ detection timestamp set
Detected --> Enqueued2 : push to Queue2
Enqueued2 --> Dequeued2 : Output pop

Dequeued2 --> OutputWritten : file/meta output written\n+ output timestamp set
OutputWritten --> ReleasedObjects : ObjectMetadataStore.release(handles)
ReleasedObjects --> ReleasedBuffer : FrameBufferStore.release(handle)
ReleasedBuffer --> ReleasedFrame : FrameMetadataStore.release(ptr)
ReleasedFrame --> [*]

note right of Enqueued1
Queue carries pointers only.\nDropOldest may drop the oldest pointer.
end note

note right of OutputWritten
Release chain is explicit:\nobject -> buffer -> frame
end note

@enduml
